### What the frontend loads on startup to build filters and translate Ids into names

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/subcategories

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/sizes

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/colors

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/genders

### ===================== PRODUCTS =====================

### All products (with sizes and stock)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### Single product
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/1

### Non-existent product -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/9999

### ===================== SCENARIO: full product lifecycle =====================
### Run in order. The Id from POST is stored in the {{productId}} variable (Rider).

### 1. Create: white polo, men's, Summer Collection, sizes M/L/XL
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Summer Pique Polo",
    "price": 129.99,
    "subcategoryId": 3,
    "colorId": 2,
    "collectionId": 2,
    "genderId": 2,
    "sizes": [
        { "sizeId": 3, "stock": 10 },
        { "sizeId": 4, "stock": 6 },
        { "sizeId": 5, "stock": 2 }
    ]
}

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. View the created product (same URL as the Location header from POST)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

### 3. Restock: price drop + new stock (XL sold out, S added)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Summer Pique Polo",
    "price": 99.99,
    "subcategoryId": 3,
    "colorId": 2,
    "collectionId": 2,
    "genderId": 2,
    "sizes": [
        { "sizeId": 2, "stock": 8 },
        { "sizeId": 3, "stock": 4 },
        { "sizeId": 4, "stock": 1 },
        { "sizeId": 5, "stock": 0 }
    ]
}

### 4. Verify the changes
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

### 5. Delete (the product's sizes are deleted with it)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

### 6. After deletion -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

### ===================== EDGE CASES =====================

### Product without a collection (collectionId = null) and without sizes
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Plain Black Gloves",
    "price": 29.99,
    "subcategoryId": 4,
    "colorId": 1,
    "collectionId": null,
    "genderId": 3,
    "sizes": []
}

### New color with a hex code
POST {{baseUrl}}/colors
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Burgundy",
    "hexCode": "#800020"
}

### Update a non-existent record -> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/genders/9999
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Kids"
}

### Non-existent color (colorId = 9999) -> currently 500 (foreign key error). To be handled with validation later.
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Ghost Product",
    "price": 10.00,
    "subcategoryId": 1,
    "colorId": 9999,
    "collectionId": null,
    "genderId": 1,
    "sizes": []
}

### Wrong data type (price as text) -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Broken Product",
    "price": "cheap",
    "subcategoryId": 1,
    "colorId": 1,
    "collectionId": null,
    "genderId": 1,
    "sizes": []
}
